  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found it. Harborview Supplies' invoice #4471 for October pallets was caught by the spam filter. I've asked for it to be released, and once a technician approves that, it will show up in your inbox. Could you reply to let me know when it arrives? One more thing: your account is locked right now after several wrong password attempts this morning. If that was you and you can't sign in, just tell us and we'll help you get unlocked. Separately, the filter also stopped a 'Scanned document 0931.zip' email because it contained malware. That one will stay blocked, so please don't ask the sender to resend it unless you were expecting it and can confirm with them some other way.",
  "internal_note": "User: Tom Becker (id 4, Finance). Checked quarantine: Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example, subject 'Invoice #4471 - October pallets', reason spam, releasable. The sender domain matches the vendor the user named and I saw no look-alike characters. The user's ticket says he expected this exact invoice, which covers KB-007's confirmation step. Release of Q-1004 is queued (approval id 1) and has not run yet. Q-1005 (scanner@docs-share.example, .zip, malware) was not released and stays quarantined. Side finding: the account status is locked with 5 failed_password attempts on 2026-10-09 between 10:12 and 10:27 ET. All came from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York during his usual hours, and earlier sign-ins from the same IP succeeded with Duo. This looks like the user mistyping, not an attack. The user didn't ask for an unlock, so I didn't queue one. I mentioned it in the reply, and we can unlock if he confirms it was him. No escalation needed.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
